{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall sanctify yourselves and you shall be holy.</b> HaShem commands that they incline toward the aspect of holiness, and thereby He promises them that they will attain the level of angels, who are called holy, as it is written (Daniel 8:13): ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֶחָד קָדוֹשׁ״ — and this is what He says: <b>and you shall be holy.</b> And you will find that they of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 20) on the verse ״כָּעֵת יֵאָמֵר לְיַעֲקֹב״ etc., that the angels stand in the outer row and Israel within, and the angels of Elohim ask His holy people: ״מַה פָּעַל אֵל״. You thus find that His holy ones, in the place of the angels, are Israel. And the verse returned and explained the matter through which they become sanctified, saying <b>and you shall keep My statutes</b> — meaning, you shall keep negative commandments and fulfill positive commandments; through this I sanctify you, for through this the name YHWH is revealed upon it, and through this one becomes sanctified — as is written in the Zohar (Tikkunim 70), that the limb through which one performs a commandment, the name YHWH alluded to in the word מִצְוָה rests upon it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:56.673906841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}